{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.88,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R4"],
      "pins": ["R4.1", "R4.2"],
      "nets": ["I2C_SCL", "+3V3"],
      "observed": "R4, the main-bus I2C SCL pull-up to +3V3, carries value \"2M2\" (2.2 MΩ) in the netlist, and the SPICE deck models it as 2.2 Meg. Its own library part, PN and description, however, are 2.2 kΩ (PN RC0805FR-072K2L, \"2.2 kOhms\"). The companion SDA pull-up R3 is correctly \"2k2\" (2.2 kΩ).",
      "expected": "R4 should be 2.2 kΩ, matching R3 and the specification's stated main-bus pull-up value.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "I2C pull-ups (R3, R4, 2.2 kΩ) for the main (non-isolated) I2C bus"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"R4\")\n      (value \"2M2\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(field (name \"Description\") \"2.2 kOhms ±1% 0.125W, 1/8W Chip Resistor 0805 (2012 Metric) Moisture Resistant Thick Film\")"},
        {"source": "spice", "quote": "R4 I2C_SCL +3V3 2.2Meg"}
      ],
      "impact": "The main I2C SCL line is pulled up by 2.2 MΩ instead of 2.2 kΩ (~1000× too weak), giving SCL rise times of hundreds of microseconds. The main bus (EZO-RTD and the primary sides of the U3/U4 ADM3260 isolators that bridge to the pH/EC EZOs) will not meet I2C timing, so pH/EC/RTD communication will be unreliable or fail entirely.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain one clear deviation: the main I2C SCL pull-up R4 is specified as 2.2 MΩ (value \"2M2\", modeled as 2.2Meg) instead of the 2.2 kΩ required by the spec and by its own part number/description and by its SDA counterpart R3, which would cripple the main I2C bus."
}

